(7  XIAO ESP32C3 \(5 V side, GND\) + BOOT / BLANK SWITCH + branch status inputs) Tj
ET
7.20 w
BT
/F2 7.204290898601705 Tf
8.00 TL
0.000 g
14.40 813.16 Td
(The XIAO now runs from +5V through the single Schottky D3 \(the XIAO needs an external diode on its 5V pin; D3 also stops its programming USB feeding the rail\). No isolated supply any more:) Tj
ET
7.20 w
BT
/F2 7.204290898601705 Tf
8.00 TL
0.000 g
14.40 803.08 Td
(XIAO ground = GND.) Tj
ET
7.20 w
BT
/F2 7.204290898601705 Tf
8.00 TL
0.000 g
14.40 793.00 Td
(GPIO map: DIN = D1 \(GPIO3\), CLK = D2 \(GPIO4\), OE = D3 \(GPIO5\), HV_EN = D10 \(GPIO10\), branch PE_OK = D4 \(GPIO6\), branch PE_FLT_N = D5 \(GPIO7\). S1A ON: GPIO9 to GND through 1k = download mode.) Tj
ET
7.20 w
BT
/F2 7.204290898601705 Tf
8.00 TL
0.000 g
14.40 782.92 Td
(S1B ON = BLANK: D5/D6 clamp the OE and HV_EN opto LED anodes, so those two lines go low whatever the GPIOs do.) Tj
ET
7.20 w
BT
/F2 7.204290898601705 Tf
8.00 TL
0.000 g
14.40 772.84 Td
(Do not connect the XIAO's USB-C and a grounded bench supply carelessly: with no isolation on the 5 V side, GND is the USB ground.) Tj
